a16z-wonderschool:greenhouse:6573786003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Wonderschool&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wonderschool’s mission is to ensure every child has access to early education that helps them realize their full potential. We do this by helping providers - small business owners who run in-home child care programs - start, operate, and grow their businesses with powerful software, coaching, and support. We also partner with governments to modernize the public child care system. Our team is small, in-person, and deeply motivated by the impact we have on families and communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an AI-focused Product Manager to own one of the most critical experiences in our platform: provider onboarding and activation. This is not a traditional PM role. You will be hands-on with customers every day - understanding their problems firsthand, translating those insights into product flows powered by AI, and shipping improvements fast. You will own the full loop from customer conversation to deployed product change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has a CS degree and has gone to business school - someone who can think technically, communicate clearly with engineers, and bring structured thinking to ambiguous customer problems. You should be comfortable using AI tools to accelerate your own work and excited about embedding AI into every layer of the customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring for two locations: &lt;strong&gt;Columbus, Ohio&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, California&lt;/strong&gt;. Both roles are in-person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend the majority of your time directly with customers - onboarding them, listening to their friction, and building trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer insights into AI-powered product flows that reduce manual effort and support intervention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship product improvements quickly, often using AI to prototype and accelerate development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build intuitive onboarding experiences that guide providers to success without requiring support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to automate repetitive steps in the onboarding and activation process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and operations to scale what works and eliminate what doesn’t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull and analyze your own data to prioritize where to focus and measure what you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providers complete onboarding faster and with less friction, measured week over week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-driven flows replace manual onboarding steps across key parts of the experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NPS of 9.5–10 or CSAT of 4.8–5 from onboarded providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;80% or more of onboarded providers convert to paying customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;50% or more of providers earn $150 or more per month within 60 days of onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Near-zero support tickets and zero manual intervention needed per provider on average&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in computer science (undergraduate CS degree required); business school or MBA strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product thinker who is energized by direct customer work - not behind a screen, but in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in AI tools and excited about using them to build better product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read and write code well enough to collaborate closely with engineers and prototype quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can turn messy customer conversations into crisp product specs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous, high-judgment, and comfortable shipping imperfect things fast and iterating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-person and energized by fast-paced, high-impact environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply motivated by helping small business owners and families&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Locations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Columbus, Ohio&lt;/strong&gt; - in-person&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, California&lt;/strong&gt; - in-person, 5-6 days a week in our office in Rincon Hill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct impact on families, small business owners, and communities every day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the CEO and leadership team on one of the company’s top priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be at the forefront of applying AI to a real, high-stakes customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy, ownership, and visibility from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a small, fast-moving team that values action over process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are expected to use agentic tools like Claude Code, Hermes, and OpenClaw to build loops that automate the product management cycle - gathering feedback, developing prototypes, running tests, and shipping to production - both on your own and with your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You go where customers are to learn. That means showing up at events on nights and weekends when needed - farmers markets, parent events, and community gatherings - and doing the work to understand customers firsthand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:6575050003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Zipline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you want to change the world? Zipline is on a mission to transform the way goods move. Our aim is to solve the world’s most urgent and complex access challenges by building, manufacturing and operating the first instant delivery and logistics system that serves all humans equally, wherever they are. From powering Rwanda’s national blood delivery network and Ghana’s COVID-19 vaccine distribution, to providing on-demand home delivery for Walmart, to enabling healthcare providers to bring care directly to U.S. homes, we are transforming the way things move for businesses, governments and consumers. The technology is complex but the idea is simple: a teleportation service that delivers what you need, when you need it. Through our technology that includes robotics and autonomy, we are decarbonizing delivery, decreasing road congestion, and reducing fossil fuel consumption and air pollution, while providing equitable access to billions of people and building a more resilient global supply chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Zipline and help us to make good on our promise to build an equitable and more resilient global supply chain for billions of people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Electrical Engineer will develop power electronics focused avionics for our next generation aircraft. We are looking for an engineer with a strong foundation in board level design and an excellent grasp of electronics development, processes, and tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Electrical Engineer on the Powertrain team, you will be responsible for architecting and designing electronics including motor inverters, power distribution, battery management, fail-safe / safety, and communication and networking systems. These components are at the core of a new unmanned aerial system that will enable Zipline’s impact to expand from 100,000 deliveries a year to 100 million across the globe. In addition, you will have the opportunity to collaborate with world class engineers across all disciplines and experience levels. Zipline values personal development highly and encourages an environment of continuous learning and mentorship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Powertrain team encounters many challenges when designing robust systems to provide life-saving service in some of the harshest environments on Earth. At the start of any project, our team plays a vital role in system architecture, designing for performance, reliability, and fault tolerance, while balancing mass and cost. Included in this is the design of an FAA-approved safety system to ensure the safety of employees, customers, and bystanders. Our sophisticated flight systems also require us to build custom solutions with high performance embedded computing and high speed serial buses. To achieve Zipline’s goal of serving anyone anywhere, all aspects of a design must be successful in a wide range of real-world environments. This means that our team is responsible for designs that are robust to broad ambient temperature ranges, can survive challenging waterproofing/ingress constraints, and maintain immunity to RF and ESD threats. These are just some of the many challenges that make us excited to go to work everyday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer avionics for volume production through a full design cycle including requirements, prototype, schematic capture, layout, and validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the architecture of Zipline’s next generation product, making impactful design decisions daily, while working with a high level of independence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead trade studies, understand competing design priorities, and provide direction and clarity for burning down risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively seek out opportunities for improvement in system, vehicle, and component level design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally in all stages of development, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecture: fault tolerance, power, mass, thermals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detailed Design: schematic capture, PCB layout, system integration, validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production: quality, failure analysis, manufacturing, cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deployment: troubleshoot field issues, develop rapid mitigations, roll learnings into future design revisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in Electrical Engineering, Embedded Hardware Engineering or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of design experience including: circuit analysis, schematic capture, PCB layout, packaging, and integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past success developing electronics for critical systems in fields such as aerospace, transportation, or medical devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with at least some of these desired:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hard-switching power converters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resonant power converters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motor drives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voltage, current, and temperature sensing analog front ends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simple digital logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic embedded communications busses (e.g. SPI, I2C, UART, CAN)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Higher speed communications (e.g. Ethernet, LVDS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for working in a fast-paced,&amp;nbsp; collaborative, cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills and the ability to explain technical challenges to both fellow engineers and non-engineers alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be eligible to work in the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work at Zipline’s South San Francisco office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: experience with practical aspects of carrying a design into mass production. This includes optimizing for cost, manufacturability, and yields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need to Know&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $160,000 - $225,000. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

